      {
        "id": "ROM.7.11-ROM.8.7",
        "orgId": "ROM.7.11-ROM.8.7",
        "bibleId": "01b29f4b342acc35-01",
        "bookId": "ROM",
        "chapterIds": [
          "ROM.7",
          "ROM.8"
        ],
        "reference": "Romans 7:11-8:7",
        "content": [
          {
            "name": "para",
            "type": "tag",
            "attrs": {
              "style": "p"
            },
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "for sin, having received an opportunity, through the command, deceived me, and through it, slew [me], ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.11",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.11"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "so that the Law, indeed, [is] holy, and the command holy, and righteous, and good. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.12",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.12"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "That which is good then, has it become death to me? Let it not be! But sin, that it might appear sin, through the good, working death to me, that sin might become exceedingly sinful through the command. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.13",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.13"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "For we have known that the Law is spiritual, and I am fleshly, sold by sin; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.14",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.14"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for that which I work, I do not acknowledge; for not what I will, this I practice, but what I hate, this I do. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.15",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.15"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And if what I do not will, this I do, I consent to the Law that [it is] good, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.16",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.16"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "and now it is no longer I that work it, but sin dwelling in me, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.17",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.17"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for I have known that there does not dwell in me, that is, in my flesh, good: for to will is present with me, and I do not find to work that which is right, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.18",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.18"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for the good that I will, I do not do; but the evil that I do not will, this I practice. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.19",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.19"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And if what I do not will, this I do, it is no longer I that work it, but sin that is dwelling in me. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.20",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.20"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "I find, then, the law, that when I desire to do what is right, the evil is present with me, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.21",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.21"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for I delight in the Law of God according to the inward man, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.22",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.22"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "and I behold another law in my members, warring against the law of my mind, and bringing me into captivity to the law of sin that [is] in my members. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.23",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.23"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "A wretched man I [am]! Who will deliver me out of the body of this death? ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.24",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.24"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "I thank God—through Jesus Christ our Lord; so then, I myself indeed serve the Law of God with the mind, and with the flesh, the law of sin.",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.7.25",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.7.25"
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "para",
            "type": "tag",
            "attrs": {
              "style": "p"
            },
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "There is, then, now no condemnation to those in Christ Jesus, who walk not according to the flesh, but according to the Spirit; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.1",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.1"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for the law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus set me free from the law of sin and of death; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.2",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.2"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for what the Law was not able to do, in that it was weak through the flesh, God, His own Son having sent in the likeness of sinful flesh, and for sin, condemned sin in the flesh, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.3",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.3"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "that the righteousness of the Law may be fulfilled in us, who do not walk according to the flesh, but according to the Spirit. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.4",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.4"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "For those who are according to the flesh, mind the things of the flesh; and those according to the Spirit, the things of the Spirit; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.5",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.5"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for the mind of the flesh [is] death, and the mind of the Spirit—life and peace; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.6",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.6"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "because the mind of the flesh [is] enmity to God, for to the Law of God it does not subject itself, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.7",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.7"
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
